{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#750","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#750","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#750\",\"parent_revision\":\"9d3b686909214d7aa112a5f44b031554ce0d518897d4f6dc6a18dc4ffced67e5\",\"root_revision\":\"9d3b686909214d7aa112a5f44b031554ce0d518897d4f6dc6a18dc4ffced67e5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `skill-creator` SKILL.md exists and is extensible | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/` |\\n| 2 | Existing cross-skill workflow examples in the repo | AVAILABLE | work-backlog-item calls groom-backlog-item + implement-feature |\\n| 3 | Skill invocation syntax (how to reference a skill from a different plugin) | AVAILABLE | CLAUDE.md reference notation section |\\n| 4 | Artifact passing between skills (conventions) | DERIVABLE | Inspect SAM task files and implement-feature delegation patterns |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information available or derivable.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Documentation-only. No code changes. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/` contains a new reference file or section covering skill composition\\n- At least 2 concrete composition templates documented: (a) linear pipeline (Skill A \u2192 Skill B \u2192 Skill C), (b) fan-out/fan-in (orchestrator spawns multiple skills in parallel, collects results)\\n- Real example from this repo used as illustration (e.g., research-curator + backlog + implement-feature)\\n- Cross-domain skill invocation syntax documented (how to call a skill from a different plugin namespace)\\n- Coordination patterns documented: how to pass artifacts between skill invocations\\n- No guidance invented \u2014 all patterns verified against actual skill behavior in the repo\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/skill-composition.md` \u2014 new composition templates reference\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md` \u2014 add link to composition reference\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an agent or developer using multiple skills together, I need skill composition templates in the skill-creator skill so I have reference patterns for chaining skill invocations across domains into compound workflows.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: Grep for \\\"Skill Composition\\\" in plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/ \u2014 at least one match. The matched file contains at least 2 concrete multi-skill workflow examples using Skill() invocations with real skill names from this repo.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add skill composition templates to skill-creator \u2014 document patterns for combining multiple skills in compound workflows** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/claude-scientific-skills.md \u2014 pattern: Bundled cross-domain examples showing multi-step workflow composition across skill domains\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe skill-creator skill (plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md) documents how to create individual skills but contains no guidance on composing multiple skills into compound workflows. No file in the repository provides skill composition templates or multi-skill workflow examples. Agents creating or using skills have no reference for how to chain skill invocations across domains (e.g., research-curator + backlog + implement-feature as a compound pipeline).\\n\\nGrep for \\\"skill-composition\\\", \\\"cross-domain\\\", and \\\"compound workflow\\\" across .claude/ returned zero results. The external-pattern-integrator skill handles integrating external patterns into local skills but does not address composing local skills together.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe skill-creator SKILL.md (or a new references/skill-composition-patterns.md file within the skill-creator skill directory) contains:\\n\\n1. A \\\"Skill Composition Patterns\\\" section with 2-3 concrete examples showing how to invoke multiple skills in sequence within a single agent workflow\\n2. Each example names specific skills from this repo (not hypothetical ones) and shows the Skill() invocation sequence\\n3. Guidance on when to compose skills vs. create a new skill that subsumes the workflow\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"630efb19c205ad9954ed21694a3095faddacda6fbde19ad0c7470d88b8df9d8d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEJxg\"}"}